From 6ea394208f5415ac7813c915b4983a302248b850 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: maan2003 <manmeetmann2003@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 18:42:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] libexpr: record observed reads of mounted local inputs; C
 API for eval settings

With record-input-reads, mounted local inputs are wrapped in an accessor that
reports what each read observed (BLAKE3 of contents and listings, stat types,
symlink targets) as eval effects, so a caller can validate a cached result
against exactly what the evaluator read. The accessor hides its fingerprint
and physical path so copies are always walked through it.

nix_eval_state_builder_eval_settings_as_abstract_settings lets C API users
set evaluator settings such as pure-eval. HashSink takes experimental-feature
settings like hashString, so observations can use BLAKE3 without enabling
blake3-hashes for user code.
---
